## Project stage upkeep

Whenever any skill starts or advances a **project** (a `plan/<slug>/` effort), set that project's `Stage:` and regenerate [[plan/index.md]] per [[doc/agents/project-status.md]]. Create `project.md` if the effort lacks one.

Starting or advancing a project follows [[.cursor/skills/project-work/SKILL.md]]. Git: [[.cursor/skills/git-protocol/SKILL.md]].

If `project.md` is `Stage: grilling` when you start or advance that project, follow [[.agents/skills/grilling/SKILL.md]] before any implement or ticket work. After grilling starts, set `charting`. Other stages are status-only. An agent already working a different issue of the same project does not stop.

An issue with `Status:` or `Stage:` `grilling` is the same directive for that issue. Do not implement it until the grill is done. Other issues in the same project do not stop.

Skill-to-stage transitions:

- `/grilling`, `/grill-with-docs`, `/wayfinder` charting a new effort → `charting`
- `/wayfinder` whose destination is a standing Roadmap (Epics, not a bounded spec) → `steering`
- `/to-spec`, a locked refactor plan, or a resolved wayfinder destination → `spec`
- `/to-tickets` → `tickets`
- implementation underway → `active`; delivered → `done`
- waiting on a named dependency or decision → `blocked`
- retired without delivery → `dead`
